<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
Hiya, Will. Was good seeing ya on Bertoxx yesterday. Even tho my connection was so horrible. I heard that the train in baltimore that caught fire actually melted some fiber optic cables, that may of been the cause.<BR>I have been trying to think of the best class for you but I think we need more input on what you want.<BR>1. Ability to solo up to level 30<BR>2. Ability to solo after 30<BR>3. Usefulness in a group<BR>4.Ability to take care of ones self<BR>5. ability to move around easily ( sow invis etc)<BR>6. Ports<BR>7. Easy of finding groups<BR>8. Melee caster healer or hybrid<BR>9. good or evil or iksar<P><BR>Some thoughts that I had<BR>-Iksar ShadowKnight- Pretty useful the whole game. Evil, but has self invisibility. Feign Death spell is good. Proble is spells arent too effective besides fear, they always seem a bit weak for level you get them. Cant dual wield so damage output isnt that great.<P>-Magician- Pretty powerful and useful in a group. Pet can be a liability. Sleethr would know more about mages tho.<P>-Warrior- They can take a beating and are considered a required class at higher levels. But there are a lot of drawbacks. You are COMPLETELY dependant on others to help you travel and heal you up. Given good gear you can fly through lower levels, but at about level25 you will not be able to solo. From about 15 to 25 you can solo, but getting healed is a pain. If you choose a melee I will play my iksar shammy to hunt with you.<P>-Druid- Awesome class. but everyone and their mom has one. Actually most people's mom has two.<P>-Shaman- Great class. Ghall would have the best input on this.<P>-Enchanter- You think your a good eq player? This will test your limits. A required class and guaranteed a group. Most of what they do is "mez" monsters to put them on hold. This is a huge agro and poor groups will get you killed very quikly. Also their power isnt appreciated until a bit later in the game. But then you will be begged to join the group<P>-Cleric- A required class after level 40ish. Sit med, stand heal. Repeat. After level 50 few groups hunt without a cleric in their group. They arent very self sufficient tho, as they dont have invis or sow. Can be very rewarding if you like healing.<P>I am gonna take a breather now and get some work done. Hopefully others will fill in other classes and offer advice.
</FONT>
