<HR size="1" color="#5d7790">
<FONT SIZE="2" FACE="Verdana, Helvetica, sans-serif">
First off,  Everquest is a group centric game.  The highier level you get, the more you need groups to get anything done.<P>If I could take what I know now and start from scratch...I'd probably make a Cleric, Enchanter or Rogue.  Probably a cleric though.<P>Mostly due to the high level game.  If you have no desire to ever hit 46+ and do raids/high-end encounters, then ANY class is great from 1-50.  It's the 50+ game that is VERY specialized.<P>It really really sucks to have a class that you loved 1-50 hit that glass ceiling when it comes to finding groups and getting exp in the post 50 game.  <P><B>From the groupable side:</B><P>Clerics: Every 40+ group needs one.  Figure a typical raid has 3-7 groups...that's at least 3-7 slots available and an extra cleric or two is always welcome.  Tanks just have too many HP for druids and Shaman to heal them effectivly past the low to mid 30's and their Rezz spell line is in VERY high demand.  Their Nukes kinda stink, but their stuns are very handy for a defensive/offensive punch.  At least, they help me keep from getting bored with the sit, heal, sit routine many clerics seem to suffer thru.<P>Enchanters: Every raid needs at least one.  Preferrably 2-3...but the high end game has some high magic resists and un-mezzable mobs, reducing Enchanters to buff machines. Not a role they enjoy for some reason..especially after being so spoiled.  Still...VERY easy to find groups as an enchanter from 16+.  Due to the high aggro their spells cause, they do die allot though...learn to be very picky with your groups.<P>Warriors: Every group needs at least one and preferably two tanks..  Warriors are the best at that job.  SK's and Pallies can tank too, just not as well and as a result sit a notch lower on the melee ratings scale.<P>Rogues: Every group loves to have one.  High Dmg output means that your group will be getting some of the exp during a raid and the monsters will drop much faster.  Pick Locks and now that traps are being implemented are also nice to have a rogue around for.<P>Shaman: Every raid needs at least one shaman...preferrably 2-3.  Slows, Debuffs and their melee buffs are very popular.<P>Monk: Every raid needs 2-3 of these too.  High dmg, but low HP/AC. They are the masters at pulling...at least they think so.  Feign Death is their number one reason.  Only they and SK's can abort a bad pull via FD and thus save the raid.<P>Wizard: Fast and High Damage with nukes that can hit even the hardest mobs.  Ports and Evacs are very nice to have.  They have some issues regarding dmg output and do suffer some in the group desirability...but still a nice class to have on a raid.<P>Shadow Knights & Paladins: Make good tanks and have some nice abilities to see them thru tuff fights.  SK's are more offensive with their spell line up while Paladins are more Defensive.  Hitpoints and AC are close to a Warrior's, but due to not having Dual Weld ( two handed fighting ) and the real nice warrior Disciplines, their melee dmg is no where close.  As a result, they have a much harder time maintaining aggro then a real warrior would.  I'd probably go with an SK over a Paladin, but that's just me.   <IMG SRC="smile.gif" border="0"><P>Bards: Jack of All Trades, but not really good at any one thing.  Overall, I'd have to say a very fun class to play and great in exp groups, but raid wise...they kinda suck.  Pre-Kunark and the lvl 50 cap, they were very popular due to their resist songs.  Now that resist gear is so easy to get and most uber-monster resists are level based...Bards are suffering a little.  They can solo pretty well once 27th via charm and their run song makes it super easy to get out of trouble fast.  I see a lot of groups shouting that they need an enchanter/bard...so if you are a good bard and make some friends as you level up, you can go far.<P>Druids: Nice class with ports, heals, buffs, and nukes...but due to that, there are a TON of them.  They can level pretty darn fast 1-50, but it does get a tad hard for a 50+ druid that suddenly sees the light and wants to start grouping/raiding.<P>Necro's: Great solo class.  They even have some nice group spells.  Just most necro's feel a tad unwanted and their raid role as a mana pump isn't what they signed up for when they rolled up their necro.<P>Magicians: Nice solo class with great pets to help you along and strong nukes.  Some good and usefull summons with some good group spells.  Main problem with this class 50+ are the pets.  Mage is balanced on their pets, but most raids are "no pets" due to aggro or pathing issues. Turning a mage into a weak wizard ( if they can hit the mob ) and mod rod dispenser.  55th is where Mages start to be wanted in raids and that is for one spell and one spell only...Call of the Hero.  Summons group member to you.  Very good for calling up late people to a raid deep inside a dungeon and used to call a puller back from certain death.  Has some limitations and was recently nerfed..so be wary about hitching your wagon to that one spell.<P>Ranger: Umm...pre-40th they are nice, but high damage output and low AC with low HP have given them a "Mana Sponge" label due to mobs getting mad at them and trying ( succeeding most of the time ) to kill them.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
</FONT>
