Goto eq.castersrealm.com when it comes time to make the character.  Their recommendations for stats are usually pretty good...at least you won't end up with a "hopeless" character that way.<P>Always..no matter what class...AGI &gt;= 75<P>Thing to remember for melee chars...STR gear is dead easy to get...STA gear is priceless. Might want to sacrifice some STR for STA in the creation process.<P>Erudite is actually a good enchanter race...too darn many HE enchanters out there.  Pretty much any race that can be a class, is a good race.  Go with a race/class combo that sound interesting.  Don't know how much Roleplay comes into the decision, but I've found DE's, Ogres & Dwarves to be the best for roleplay.  DE's for their "Evil" god and bloodlust, Ogres for their "Dumbness" and Dwarves for being Drunks.<P>Rogue...Dorfs are good too, small size and night vision are nice to have.  The mask kinda makes up for that later...but again..STR & STA pretty important.<P>Iksar are darn nice...regen and medium size..handy on those dungeon crawls where shrinks aren't available.<P>--------------------<P>Verser - Bard of the 51st Song
